-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  exe_cli_options.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: pcpp -h

  pcpp -h lists every option with what it does, then examples (exit 0).

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp -h
  EXPECT:
    PaskalCPP™ CLI v<VERSION>
    Copyright © 2026-present tinyBigGAMES™ LLC, All Rights Reserved.
    https://paskalcpp.org

    USAGE:
      pcpp <source> [OPTIONS]
      pcpp --clean [<folder>] [--dry-run]

    REQUIRED:
      <source>                  Main module (.pcpp)

    OPTIONS:
      -r, --run                    Run after building (executables only)
      -o, --output    <path>       Set output directory (wins over @outputpath; default: output)
      -t, --target    <triple>     Set target triple: x86_64-windows-gnu (default), x86_64-linux-gnu
      -opt, --optimize <level>     Set optimize level: debug, safe, fast, small
      --defaults                   -opt / -t only apply where the source has no @optimize / @target (the editor passes this)
      --progress                   Draw the build progress in place even when output is piped (the editor passes this)
      --terminal      <pipe>       With -r: the program's terminal is the named pipe an editor listens on
      editor [files]               Start the PaskalCPP Editor with the files given
      -d, --debug                  Build debug, then debug it in the console debugger (x86_64-windows-gnu)
      --host          <exe>        With -d on a dll: the exe that loads it
      -- <args>                    Everything after -- is passed, as written, to the program -r or -d runs
      --lsp                        Run the language server on stdin/stdout (takes no other argument)
      --dap                        Run the debug adapter (DAP) on stdin/stdout (takes no other argument)
      --clean         [<folder>]   Clear a pcpp output folder (default: the current folder), after checks and a y/N question
      --dry-run                    With --clean: check and list what would be deleted, delete nothing
      -h, --help                   Display this help message

    EXAMPLES:
      pcpp hello
      pcpp hello -r
      pcpp hello -r -opt fast
      pcpp hello -d
      pcpp hello --target x86_64-linux-gnu --output build
      pcpp editor hello.pcpp
      pcpp --clean output --dry-run
  EXITCODE: 0
  <VERSION> is the compiler's version (the banner's one changing text); the
  tester runs pcpp.exe itself (cmCli), once: the CLI is the same for every
  target. This file is not compiled.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe exe_cli_options;

begin
end.
